menu "feckless_graphics_handler"

    config FECKLESS_GFX_BLIT_STATS
        bool "Log where gfx_blit()'s time goes (diagnostic)"
        default n
        help
            u-feckless-0032. Every 100 blits, logs the average blit and its
            parts: waiting for the blit lock, the brightness filter's copy
            into the scratch, esp_lcd_panel_draw_bitmap() (retries
            included), waiting for the transfer to finish, and the one-tick
            gaps between the bands a big blit is split into -- with the
            bands and rows a blit averaged. Costs a timer read per part.

    config FECKLESS_GFX_BLIT_GAP_US
        int "Gap between the bands of a big blit, microseconds (0: one tick)"
        default 0
        range 0 5000
        help
            u-feckless-0033. A blit taller than 600 rows goes out in bands of
            240 with a gap between them, so the panel's own refresh DMA gets
            the bus (the flash it fixed was a whole-strip repaint). 0 keeps
            the gap as it was, vTaskDelay(1): up to a tick each, about 1 ms
            at 1000 Hz, which on Lothesome's 940-row frames is 3 ms of a 14 ms
            blit (CONFIG_FECKLESS_GFX_BLIT_STATS). A value here waits that
            many microseconds instead, on the CPU. Lower it until the panel
            flashes, then raise it.

endmenu
